{
    "background_story": "Wade was a charming restaurateur with a passion for French cuisine. After years of working in some of Paris' finest eateries, he decided to open his own brasserie in the heart of the city. 'Chez Wade' quickly became a sensation, attracting foodies and locals alike with its cozy atmosphere and mouthwatering dishes. Wade's menu was a love letter to the classic brasserie fare, with escargots, steak tartare, and confit de canard that would make even the most discerning French chef proud. But what truly set Chez Wade apart was the warm hospitality that Wade and his team extended to every guest. Regulars raved about Wade's ability to make everyone feel like family, and his brasserie became a staple of the community. As Wade would say, 'A good meal is not just about the food, it's about the company and the memories you create.'",
